259
00:20:24.807 --> 00:20:27.059
Uh. no. I just saw something
from the road.

260
00:20:27.143 --> 00:20:28.686
This isn't going to take long.

261
00:20:29.353 --> 00:20:30.271
Sure.

262
00:20:47.079 --> 00:20:48.414
Are we good?

263
00:20:49.749 --> 00:20:50.833
Yeah. we're good.

264
00:20:52.084 --> 00:20:53.711
[birds chirping]

265
00:21:16.317 --> 00:21:18.360
[man] Go ahead. check it out. Come on.

266
00:21:33.584 --> 00:21:35.795
[water dripping]

267
00:21:50.100 --> 00:21:51.018
[gasps]

268
00:22:05.199 --> 00:22:06.200
I told her...

269
00:22:07.326 --> 00:22:08.536
I don't mind if she looks.

270
00:22:11.705 --> 00:22:12.748
Who are they?

271
00:22:12.832 --> 00:22:14.166
Looters.

272
00:22:14.250 --> 00:22:16.460
[weakly] I got kids. man. [coughs]

273
00:22:17.670 --> 00:22:18.921
I actually know that guy.

274
00:22:21.048 --> 00:22:22.466
Went to high school together.

275
00:22:24.051 --> 00:22:25.344
He didn't talk to me much.

276
00:22:27.429 --> 00:22:29.056
Much more talkative now.

277
00:22:32.017 --> 00:22:34.728
We've been debating
what to do with them for two days now.

278
00:22:36.230 --> 00:22:37.606
We go around in circles.

279
00:22:37.690 --> 00:22:39.233
- [chuckles]
- [coughs]

280
00:22:39.316 --> 00:22:40.317
[gasps]

281
00:22:40.401 --> 00:22:41.485
Tell you what.

282
00:22:44.154 --> 00:22:47.366
Why don't you put us and them
out of our misery and make a call?

283
00:22:48.117 --> 00:22:49.368
I'll put rounds in them right now.

284
00:22:51.078 --> 00:22:53.205
Or we'll beat 'em up a little more.

285
00:22:54.957 --> 00:22:56.208
Strap them to the front.

286
00:22:57.084 --> 00:22:59.420
We'll let them go after a couple of days.

287
00:22:59.503 --> 00:23:01.797
[breathing heavily]

288
00:23:01.881 --> 00:23:03.674
[strained breathing]

289
00:23:03.757 --> 00:23:05.551
[chuckles]

290
00:23:06.886 --> 00:23:08.053
Flip a coin if you like.

291
00:23:11.181 --> 00:23:13.392
Would you stand with them?

292
00:23:14.184 --> 00:23:15.561
- Stand with them?
- Yeah.

293
00:23:19.899 --> 00:23:21.775
I'd like to take your picture.

294
00:23:30.492 --> 00:23:32.912
Okay. Just stand over there?

295
00:23:33.704 --> 00:23:34.622
Yeah.

296
00:23:35.289 --> 00:23:36.665
Where do you want me?

297
00:23:37.499 --> 00:23:40.502
Uh. between the two.

298
00:23:41.503 --> 00:23:42.630
Got you.

299
00:23:47.927 --> 00:23:49.386
I didn't take a photo.

300
00:23:50.596 --> 00:23:52.306
I didn't take a single photo.

301
00:23:52.389 --> 00:23:56.810
I didn't even remember a camera's on me.
Like. oh. my God. like. like.

302
00:23:56.894 --> 00:23:59.188
why didn't I just tell him
not to shoot them?

303
00:23:59.271 --> 00:24:01.440
- They're probably gonna kill them anyway.
- How do you know?

304
00:24:01.523 --> 00:24:04.151
He doesn't know.
but that's besides the point.

305
00:24:05.277 --> 00:24:08.697
Once you start asking yourself
those questions. you can't stop.

306
00:24:08.781 --> 00:24:12.159
So we don't ask.
We record so other people ask.

307
00:24:12.242 --> 00:24:14.244
Wanna be a journalist? That's the job.

308
00:24:14.328 --> 00:24:16.246
- Hey. Lee.
- What?

309
00:24:16.330 --> 00:24:17.498
Back off.

310
00:24:17.581 --> 00:24:19.083
What am I saying that's wrong?

311
00:24:19.166 --> 00:24:21.627
I'm not saying it's wrong.
she's just shook up.

312
00:24:21.710 --> 00:24:23.671
Lee doesn't understand "shook up".

313
00:24:23.754 --> 00:24:25.172
Whoa.

314
00:24:25.255 --> 00:24:27.132
I'm not being protective of her?

315
00:24:27.216 --> 00:24:29.593
You're the idiot who let her in this car.

316
00:24:31.220 --> 00:24:33.806
What happened back there
is nothing in comparison

317
00:24:33.889 --> 00:24:35.391
to what we're heading into.

318
00:24:35.474 --> 00:24:36.767
You need to understand...

319
00:24:38.143 --> 00:24:40.187
Oh. shit. she's crying.

320
00:24:41.730 --> 00:24:45.025
The back seat is both a kindergarten

321
00:24:45.109 --> 00:24:46.568
and an old people's home.

322
00:24:47.653 --> 00:24:48.696
How did this happen?

323
00:24:48.779 --> 00:24:50.781
Lee. what the fuck?

324
00:24:50.864 --> 00:24:51.949
Lee's right.

325
00:24:56.537 --> 00:24:58.247
I won't make that mistake again.

326
00:25:06.463 --> 00:25:09.008
[president on radio] ...the terms
of the so-called peace summit

327
00:25:09.091 --> 00:25:11.635
could only be rejected. truly rejected

328
00:25:11.719 --> 00:25:14.388
by all great-thinking Americans.

329
00:25:15.848 --> 00:25:18.976
To the secessionists. I say only this.

330
00:25:20.144 --> 00:25:25.691
I pledge allegiance to the flag
of the United States of America.

331
00:25:27.818 --> 00:25:31.405
We stand ready to fulfill
the promise of our forefathers.

332
00:25:31.488 --> 00:25:34.408
to the flag. to the nation.

333
00:25:35.993 --> 00:25:37.202
and to God.

334
00:25:41.665 --> 00:25:42.916
Stop here a minute.

335
00:25:44.251 --> 00:25:46.253
This seem like a good place
for a toilet break?

336
00:25:46.336 --> 00:25:47.463
Just pull in.

337
00:26:01.351 --> 00:26:02.519
[seat belt clicks]

338
00:26:02.603 --> 00:26:03.854
Come with me.

339
00:26:03.937 --> 00:26:05.105
[car door opens]

340
00:26:08.942 --> 00:26:11.111
- Come with me.
- [sighs]

341
00:26:17.201 --> 00:26:20.204
[tense music playing]

342
00:26:45.270 --> 00:26:46.271
Shoot it.

343
00:26:48.690 --> 00:26:49.733
Shoot the helicopter?

344
00:26:49.817 --> 00:26:50.734
Yeah.

345
00:26:51.693 --> 00:26:53.153
It's gonna make a good image.

346
00:27:01.245 --> 00:27:02.913
[camera shutter clicking]

347
00:27:21.890 --> 00:27:23.517
FE2s.

348
00:27:23.600 --> 00:27:25.519
You don't see them around much.

349
00:27:25.602 --> 00:27:26.812
Yeah.

350
00:27:26.895 --> 00:27:28.647
They're my dad's cameras actually.

351
00:27:30.399 --> 00:27:32.151
Don't worry. he's not dead.

352
00:27:32.234 --> 00:27:33.735
He's...

353
00:27:33.819 --> 00:27:37.447
sitting on his farm in Missouri.
pretending like none of this is happening.

354
00:27:42.411 --> 00:27:44.955
[camera shutter clicks]

355
00:27:53.922 --> 00:27:54.840
Lee.

356
00:27:56.049 --> 00:27:59.595
I'm sorry for jamming my way
into your ride. okay?

357
00:27:59.678 --> 00:28:01.388
I know you're really angry about it.

358
00:28:01.471 --> 00:28:04.266
and I know you think
I don't know shit. but...

359
00:28:04.349 --> 00:28:06.643
I'm not angry about that. Jessie.

360
00:28:06.727 --> 00:28:09.062
I don't care what you do or don't know.

361
00:28:09.146 --> 00:28:11.315
Okay. but you are angry with me.

362
00:28:11.398 --> 00:28:15.444
There is no version of this
that isn't a mistake.

363
00:28:16.445 --> 00:28:18.280
I know. because I'm it.

364
00:28:19.323 --> 00:28:20.532
Joel and Sammy are it.

365
00:28:21.825 --> 00:28:23.285
- It's my choice.
- Right.

366
00:28:24.745 --> 00:28:26.413
And I'll remember that

367
00:28:26.496 --> 00:28:30.042
when you lose your shit.
or you get blown up or shot.

368
00:28:33.712 --> 00:28:36.548
[Jessie] Would you photograph
that moment if I got shot?

369
00:28:39.092 --> 00:28:40.344
[Lee] What do you think?

370
00:28:47.142 --> 00:28:50.395
[distant gunfire]

371
00:28:52.272 --> 00:28:53.899
[distant explosion]

372
00:28:54.816 --> 00:28:57.653
Every time I survived a war zone.

373
00:28:57.736 --> 00:28:59.196
and got the photo.

374
00:29:00.405 --> 00:29:02.616
I thought I was sending a warning home.

375
00:29:03.784 --> 00:29:05.118
"Don't do this."

376
00:29:06.453 --> 00:29:07.788
But here we are.

377
00:29:10.624 --> 00:29:12.334
So it's existential.

378
00:29:13.502 --> 00:29:15.087
What is?

379
00:29:15.170 --> 00:29:16.380
What's eating you.

380
00:29:20.467 --> 00:29:22.386
Don't worry about me. Sammy.

381
00:29:25.764 --> 00:29:28.850
Am I allowed to say
I remember you at her age?

382
00:29:30.852 --> 00:29:32.104
And I wasn't so different?

383
00:29:32.187 --> 00:29:33.814
You weren't so different.

384
00:29:33.897 --> 00:29:37.818
You think you're being hard on her.
and I think you're being hard on yourself.

385
00:29:38.527 --> 00:29:41.571
- Okay. writer.
- Damn it. Lee. Stop.

386
00:29:42.781 --> 00:29:44.408
I'm speaking truth.

387
00:29:44.491 --> 00:29:47.536
And for the record. sure.
I'm worried about that girl.

388
00:29:47.619 --> 00:29:49.454
And I'm worried about you too.

389
00:29:51.832 --> 00:29:53.375
[Joel] What are you worrying
about Lee for?

390
00:29:55.585 --> 00:29:58.672
Lee's lost her faith
in the power of journalism.

391
00:29:58.755 --> 00:30:01.633
State of the nation is QED.

392
00:30:01.717 --> 00:30:04.303
I can't answer to that. Sammy.

393
00:30:04.386 --> 00:30:05.679
But I can tell you.

394
00:30:06.513 --> 00:30:08.640
this gunfire...

395
00:30:08.724 --> 00:30:11.310
is getting me extremely fucking hard.

396
00:30:11.393 --> 00:30:13.020
[distant gunfire continues]

397
00:30:13.103 --> 00:30:15.355
Look at that shit light up the sky.

398
00:30:15.439 --> 00:30:17.232
[Lee] It's not our story.

399
00:30:17.316 --> 00:30:18.984
- Yeah.
- [distant explosion]

400
00:30:19.067 --> 00:30:21.778
But you know. bang-bang.

401
00:30:21.862 --> 00:30:25.198
We're not going
anywhere near that in the dark.

402
00:30:25.282 --> 00:30:26.366
But sunup?

403
00:30:27.868 --> 00:30:30.495
If they're still at it. we'll take a look.

404
00:30:33.206 --> 00:30:34.124
[sniffs]

405
00:30:36.710 --> 00:30:37.627
Cool.

406
00:30:37.711 --> 00:30:38.920
[huffs smoke]

407
00:30:45.344 --> 00:30:46.261
Thanks.

408
00:31:03.528 --> 00:31:04.905
[bottle clinks]

409
00:31:04.988 --> 00:31:11.036
[object clacks. thuds]

410
00:31:12.245 --> 00:31:16.750
[drumming fingers]

411
00:31:16.833 --> 00:31:18.043
Action tomorrow.

412
00:31:20.504 --> 00:31:22.089
We're going down there?

413
00:31:22.172 --> 00:31:23.090
Yeah.

414
00:31:27.094 --> 00:31:28.136
But not you.

415
00:31:28.929 --> 00:31:31.598
You're gonna... You're gonna hang back.

416
00:31:33.392 --> 00:31:34.476
I don't wanna hang back.

417
00:31:34.559 --> 00:31:35.769
Oh. you have to hang back.

418
00:31:37.521 --> 00:31:39.481
I'm not hanging back.

419
00:31:42.943 --> 00:31:44.486
You should see your face.

420
00:31:44.569 --> 00:31:45.904
[Joel huffs smoke]

421
00:31:45.987 --> 00:31:47.989
Stomach doing turns. Right.

422
00:31:50.075 --> 00:31:52.411
You don't get a minute of sleep tonight.

423
00:31:53.829 --> 00:31:55.497
My advice.

424
00:31:55.580 --> 00:31:57.707
don't expect to sleep.

425
00:31:57.791 --> 00:32:00.710
That way if you do. it's a...
it's a nice surprise.

426
00:32:05.757 --> 00:32:06.800
You gonna sleep?

427
00:32:07.801 --> 00:32:08.760
[inhales]

428
00:32:10.470 --> 00:32:13.348
I got a little bit Ativan. [exhales]

429
00:32:15.642 --> 00:32:17.561
Got plenty.
I can give you some if you like.

430
00:32:18.228 --> 00:32:19.855
Uh. no. it's okay.

431
00:32:19.938 --> 00:32:20.856
Or...

432
00:32:21.731 --> 00:32:23.024
I can stay up with you.

433
00:32:23.984 --> 00:32:25.068
Keep you company.

434
00:32:27.362 --> 00:32:29.489
N-no. I...

435
00:32:29.573 --> 00:32:33.285
I don't wanna be a burden or whatever.

436
00:32:37.205 --> 00:32:38.206
Sure.

437
00:32:42.419 --> 00:32:45.797
But seriously. if you do get
freaked out or something.

438
00:32:45.881 --> 00:32:47.716
just wake me up.

439
00:32:48.925 --> 00:32:50.594
It's not nice being scared alone.

440
00:32:54.723 --> 00:32:55.807
Thanks. Joel.

441
00:32:57.434 --> 00:32:58.477
You bet. darling.

442
00:33:40.435 --> 00:33:42.187
[insects chirping]

443
00:33:42.270 --> 00:33:44.898
[soft music playing]

444
00:33:56.243 --> 00:33:59.871
[distant explosion and gunfire]

445
00:34:06.086 --> 00:34:09.047
- Get down! I said go flank the building!
- [man screaming]

446
00:34:09.130 --> 00:34:10.674
No! Fuck!

447
00:34:10.757 --> 00:34:12.968
- [screams]
- Shit!

448
00:34:13.051 --> 00:34:14.803
- [man 1] Mike. come on!
- [metal clanks]

449
00:34:14.886 --> 00:34:16.555
[camera shutter clicking]

450
00:34:16.638 --> 00:34:18.181
- [gunfire]
- [car alarm blaring]

451
00:34:18.265 --> 00:34:20.725
[Mike] Get me the fuck
out of here! Fuck!

452
00:34:20.809 --> 00:34:23.019
I said go flank the fucking building!

453
00:34:23.103 --> 00:34:24.145
Got it.

454
00:34:24.229 --> 00:34:26.606
[gunfire continues]

455
00:34:26.690 --> 00:34:27.649
Do something!

456
00:34:29.150 --> 00:34:30.235
Get ready to move.

457
00:34:30.318 --> 00:34:32.404
- Prep the smoke.
- Get me the fuck out of here!

458
00:34:35.907 --> 00:34:37.784
- Fuck!
- Smoke down!

459
00:34:40.829 --> 00:34:42.914
- [screams]
- On the count of three.

460
00:34:42.998 --> 00:34:45.584
- Three. two. one.
- [man 3] Cover mel!

461
00:34:47.419 --> 00:34:48.503
[camera shutter clicking]

462
00:34:56.011 --> 00:34:58.263
[camera shutter clicking]

463
00:34:58.346 --> 00:34:59.848
- [man 1] Watch now.
- [Mike yells] Fuck!

464
00:34:59.931 --> 00:35:01.182
- Fuck!
- Shit!

465
00:35:01.266 --> 00:35:03.101
- [man 4] Hey. man. you all right?
- [Mike] I'm gonna get hit!

466
00:35:03.184 --> 00:35:04.269
- [man 3] Go get him.
- [man 1] Yeah!

467
00:35:04.352 --> 00:35:06.479
Now. move it! You gotta move!

468
00:35:13.528 --> 00:35:15.196
[camera shutter clicking]

469
00:35:15.280 --> 00:35:17.407
Mike's down! You gotta get him!

470
00:35:17.490 --> 00:35:18.950
Mike's down.

471
00:35:23.079 --> 00:35:25.040
- Move back!
- [panting]

472
00:35:25.123 --> 00:35:26.416
Move back!

473
00:35:29.544 --> 00:35:31.087
[grunts]

474
00:35:31.171 --> 00:35:32.839
[camera shutter clicking]

475
00:35:34.174 --> 00:35:35.175
[Mike groaning]

476
00:35:35.258 --> 00:35:37.385
[man 1] I got you. Hang in.
Stay with me.

477
00:35:37.469 --> 00:35:40.930
[Mike continues groaning]

478
00:35:41.014 --> 00:35:44.267
- [man 1] Fuck! Give me gauze.
- [groaning]

479
00:35:50.523 --> 00:35:54.653
[Jessie panting]

480
00:36:08.958 --> 00:36:11.002
[distant groans]

481
00:36:44.202 --> 00:36:45.745
[groaning continues]

482
00:37:17.819 --> 00:37:19.612
[groaning continues]

483
00:37:36.921 --> 00:37:40.633
[man groaning. crying]

484
00:37:43.887 --> 00:37:46.806
[man crying]

485
00:37:46.890 --> 00:37:50.769
[man coughing. groaning]

486
00:37:58.943 --> 00:38:00.195
I need help.

487
00:38:03.573 --> 00:38:08.411
["'Say No Go" by De La Soul playing]

488
00:38:26.596 --> 00:38:31.142
["Say No Go" playing]

489
00:38:31.226 --> 00:38:35.522
[inaudible]

490
00:39:20.316 --> 00:39:23.987
[inaudible]

491
00:39:51.848 --> 00:39:55.268
[Joel] Holy fucking shit!

492
00:39:55.351 --> 00:39:57.437
What a fucking rush!

493
00:40:00.607 --> 00:40:04.569
[indistinct chatter]

494
00:40:25.965 --> 00:40:27.383
- You're press?
- [Joel] Yes. ma'am.

495
00:40:28.426 --> 00:40:29.344
IDs.

496
00:40:35.350 --> 00:40:37.268
Okay. Are you staying the night?

497
00:40:37.352 --> 00:40:38.394
Yeah. just one.

498
00:40:40.605 --> 00:40:42.315
Park over there.

499
00:40:42.398 --> 00:40:43.983
There's a canteen where you can eat.

500
00:40:44.067 --> 00:40:45.985
And no tents available.

501
00:40:46.069 --> 00:40:47.070
Thanks. ma'am.

502
00:41:01.709 --> 00:41:04.003
[children chattering]

503
00:41:12.053 --> 00:41:13.221
[Joel] You're good.

504
00:41:13.304 --> 00:41:15.723
[girl] Eight. nine. ten.

505
00:41:15.807 --> 00:41:17.976
- [Lee] Hey. get in there.
- [Joel] I'm gonna show these kids...

506
00:41:18.059 --> 00:41:19.727
- Check this out. Okay!
- [Lee laughs]

507
00:41:19.811 --> 00:41:23.439
- [boy] One. two. three. four...
- [Joel] Eleven. twelve. thirteen...

508
00:41:23.523 --> 00:41:25.858
- [kids clamor]
- [Joel laughs] Yeah.

509
00:41:25.942 --> 00:41:26.985
Your turn. Sammy.

510
00:41:28.528 --> 00:41:30.363
[boy chuckles] Hey. wait up.

511
00:41:30.446 --> 00:41:32.740
[indistinct chatter. laughter]

512
00:41:51.342 --> 00:41:53.845
- [Lee] Brought you something.
- [Jessie] Oh. thanks.

513
00:41:57.974 --> 00:41:59.225
[Lee] Don't forget to eat.

514
00:41:59.308 --> 00:42:00.518
[Jessie] Yeah. I'm starving.

515
00:42:04.147 --> 00:42:06.858
I'll eat once I handle this.

516
00:42:06.941 --> 00:42:09.694
- [clears throat]
- Developing negs on the road.

517
00:42:09.777 --> 00:42:12.030
Yeah. I got myself
a pretty neat travel kit.

518
00:42:12.947 --> 00:42:13.948
I'm impressed.

519
00:42:15.033 --> 00:42:17.368
Wanna know the secret
of getting the developer just right?

520
00:42:17.452 --> 00:42:18.453
[Lee] Hmm.

521
00:42:21.164 --> 00:42:22.373
Body temperature.

522
00:42:22.457 --> 00:42:24.292
- Smart.
- Thank you.

523
00:42:29.464 --> 00:42:35.219
So. how about you tell me the story
of how you became a photojournalist?

524
00:42:35.887 --> 00:42:37.513
You don't know?

525
00:42:37.597 --> 00:42:39.265
I thought I was one of your heroes.

526
00:42:39.348 --> 00:42:41.017
Uh... [chuckles]

527
00:42:41.100 --> 00:42:43.478
Yeah. I do.

528
00:42:43.561 --> 00:42:45.271
When you were in college.

529
00:42:45.354 --> 00:42:49.776
you took the motherfucking legendary photo
of the Antifa massacre.

530
00:42:51.360 --> 00:42:55.531
Then you became the youngest ever
Magnum photographer.

531
00:42:57.241 --> 00:43:00.036
That would be my Wikipedia page.

532
00:43:00.119 --> 00:43:01.662
But what's missing from it?

533
00:43:01.746 --> 00:43:04.290
I don't know. A lot.

534
00:43:07.293 --> 00:43:09.253
Well. that's gotta sit here
for ten minutes.

535
00:43:09.337 --> 00:43:11.089
so you might as well expand a little.

536
00:43:12.465 --> 00:43:13.716
What about your folks?

537
00:43:15.051 --> 00:43:17.970
Well. actually they're on a farm too.

538
00:43:18.054 --> 00:43:20.181
- Oh?
- Except. Colorado.

539
00:43:20.264 --> 00:43:23.017
Also pretending this isn't happening.

540
00:43:23.101 --> 00:43:25.186
[scoffs] No shit.

541
00:43:29.107 --> 00:43:32.443
Hey. these are dry.
Should we check them out?

542
00:43:32.527 --> 00:43:33.444
Sure.

543
00:43:34.320 --> 00:43:36.572
Still need a phone
even though you can't get a signal.

544
00:43:40.993 --> 00:43:41.911
[clicks]

545
00:43:47.333 --> 00:43:49.335
I don't want you to see these. Um...

546
00:43:50.294 --> 00:43:53.089
They're not even in focus.
Like... [chuckles]

547
00:43:53.172 --> 00:43:54.549
Exposure is all wrong.

548
00:43:54.632 --> 00:43:55.758
Just keep looking.

549
00:43:57.301 --> 00:44:00.721
Figure the strike rate for keepers
is 30 to one.

550
00:44:04.684 --> 00:44:06.686
[clicking]

551
00:44:26.873 --> 00:44:29.083
It's a great photo. Jessie.

552
00:44:34.338 --> 00:44:41.345
[indistinct chatter. laughter]

553
00:45:45.660 --> 00:45:50.039
[camera shutter clicking]

554
00:46:22.530 --> 00:46:24.740
[birds chirping]

555
00:46:42.967 --> 00:46:44.260
[dog barks in distance]

556
00:46:49.015 --> 00:46:51.225
Did we just drive through a time portal?

557
00:46:52.184 --> 00:46:53.936
It's The Twilight Zone.

558
00:46:56.689 --> 00:46:58.065
[dog barks]

559
00:47:03.070 --> 00:47:04.071
[engine stops]

560
00:47:19.920 --> 00:47:20.921
[doorbell dings]

561
00:47:23.758 --> 00:47:25.718
Hey there. Welcome.

562
00:47:25.801 --> 00:47:27.345
Feel free to look around.

563
00:47:41.442 --> 00:47:42.360
Hey.

564
00:47:44.362 --> 00:47:45.529
Out of interest. but...

565
00:47:47.281 --> 00:47:48.783
are you guys aware there's like a...

566
00:47:50.117 --> 00:47:53.788
pretty huge civil war going on
all across America.

567
00:47:53.871 --> 00:47:57.291
Oh. sure. but we just try to stay out.

568
00:48:02.129 --> 00:48:03.130
"Stay out"?

569
00:48:03.214 --> 00:48:06.884
With what we see on the news.
seems like it's for the best.

570
00:48:09.637 --> 00:48:10.638
Yeah.

571
00:48:10.721 --> 00:48:13.015
Well. let me know
if you wanna try anything on.

572
00:48:14.100 --> 00:48:15.017
Thanks.

573
00:48:16.977 --> 00:48:18.562
- Lee.
- Mm?

574
00:48:20.981 --> 00:48:22.108
[scoffs]

575
00:48:22.191 --> 00:48:23.234
What?

576
00:48:24.235 --> 00:48:26.404
You're so war-torn.
you can't try on a dress?

577
00:48:43.546 --> 00:48:46.090
Jesus... [clears throat]

578
00:48:46.173 --> 00:48:48.134
When you haven't seen yourself
in a mirror...

579
00:48:48.217 --> 00:48:50.428
- Oh. my God. Shut the fuck up.
- ...in a few days.

580
00:48:51.679 --> 00:48:53.556
Turn around. I wanna take your photo.

581
00:48:56.058 --> 00:48:56.976
No.

582
00:48:58.519 --> 00:48:59.562
Come on.

583
00:49:00.187 --> 00:49:01.105
Yes.

584
00:49:08.112 --> 00:49:09.238
[sighs]

585
00:49:16.620 --> 00:49:18.289
You're gonna take the photo?

586
00:49:18.372 --> 00:49:20.082
You told me not to rush.

587
00:49:20.166 --> 00:49:22.710
Yeah. but there's a sweet spot.
and you're missing it.

588
00:49:22.793 --> 00:49:24.795
Don't wanna miss your sweet spot.

589
00:49:25.421 --> 00:49:26.797
- [chuckles]
- [camera clicks]

590
00:49:26.881 --> 00:49:29.091
Well. no. that was not the moment.

591
00:49:29.925 --> 00:49:31.177
[chuckles]

592
00:49:31.260 --> 00:49:32.428
Okay.

593
00:49:32.511 --> 00:49:33.637
One more.

594
00:49:39.935 --> 00:49:41.729
- Lee.
- Yes.

595
00:49:41.812 --> 00:49:42.980
You're pretty when you smile.

596
00:49:43.063 --> 00:49:45.399
- [light chuckle]
- [camera shutter clicks]

597
00:49:45.483 --> 00:49:47.276
- [whirs. clicks]
- There you go.

598
00:49:48.444 --> 00:49:49.612
[Joel] Hey.

599
00:49:51.989 --> 00:49:53.032
How about this?

600
00:49:54.408 --> 00:49:55.910
Yeah. nice.

601
00:49:58.245 --> 00:49:59.538
Not gonna take a picture?

602
00:49:59.622 --> 00:50:00.706
Right.

603
00:50:01.790 --> 00:50:04.793
You know what. though.
running a little low on film.

604
00:50:07.588 --> 00:50:09.673
You're mean. I'm out.

605
00:50:09.757 --> 00:50:10.758
[Jessie chuckles]

606
00:50:12.927 --> 00:50:14.136
- [door opens]
- [doorbell dings]

607
00:50:16.138 --> 00:50:17.473
I'm gonna go try this on.

608
00:50:19.683 --> 00:50:20.601
[door closes]

609
00:50:25.564 --> 00:50:26.482
[doorbell dings]

610
00:50:31.946 --> 00:50:33.739
You actually bought something?

611
00:50:33.822 --> 00:50:34.740
[Lee scoffs]

612
00:50:36.951 --> 00:50:39.245
She did. She's paying now.

613
00:50:41.247 --> 00:50:43.207
[inhales deeply]

614
00:50:43.290 --> 00:50:44.333
It's so weird.

615
00:50:45.334 --> 00:50:47.795
This place is like everything
I'd forgotten.

616
00:50:48.587 --> 00:50:52.591
Funny. I was thinking it felt like
everything I remembered.

617
00:50:54.843 --> 00:50:56.887
Look at the tops of the buildings.

618
00:50:56.971 --> 00:50:58.013
Be subtle.

619
00:51:14.280 --> 00:51:16.240
Wouldn't have suited us anyway. Lee.

620
00:51:17.408 --> 00:51:18.951
We'd have gotten bored.

621
00:51:19.034 --> 00:51:20.327
[Lee scoffs]

622
00:51:20.578 --> 00:51:24.873
[president on radio] / remain ready
to accept the full immediate

623
00:51:24.957 --> 00:51:28.711
and unconditional surrender
of the secessionist forces.

624
00:51:28.794 --> 00:51:32.506
To liberate the people
of the subjugated states

625
00:51:32.590 --> 00:51:34.842
and start rebuilding our great nation.

626
00:51:34.925 --> 00:51:36.510
[Sammy] Enough of this shit.

627
00:51:36.594 --> 00:51:39.722
- [clicks]
- Words might as well be random.

628
00:51:39.805 --> 00:51:43.392
What do you think he'll actually say
if I do get a microphone over to him?

629
00:51:43.475 --> 00:51:45.060
Not much.

630
00:51:45.144 --> 00:51:49.481
The ones that get taken.
Gaddafi. Mussolini. Ceausescu.

631
00:51:49.565 --> 00:51:52.067
they're always lesser men than you think.

632
00:51:52.151 --> 00:51:54.445
At the end. they let you down. Joel.

633
00:51:54.528 --> 00:51:56.905
Just as long as he isn't dead
before I get there.

634
00:52:09.126 --> 00:52:10.127
Hold up.

635
00:52:10.210 --> 00:52:13.839
[christmas music playing]

636
00:52:39.239 --> 00:52:41.367
There was a turnoff
three or four miles back.

637
00:52:41.450 --> 00:52:44.286
Maybe we should turn around.
take another route.

638
00:52:44.370 --> 00:52:45.537
Can you see anything?

639
00:52:45.621 --> 00:52:47.039
- No.
- [clicks]

640
00:52:47.998 --> 00:52:51.001
[Joel] Nothing. no shapes.
no movement. nothing?

641
00:52:52.753 --> 00:52:53.671
No.

642
00:52:56.298 --> 00:52:58.509
Okay. I'm gonna drive forward a little.

643
00:53:01.053 --> 00:53:04.807
[christmas music continues playing]

644
00:53:25.369 --> 00:53:26.662
Should we keep going?

645
00:53:26.745 --> 00:53:28.330
[gunshots]

646
00:53:28.414 --> 00:53:29.540
Shit!

647
00:53:29.623 --> 00:53:31.208
[tires screeching]

648
00:53:35.254 --> 00:53:36.839
[tires screeching]

649
00:53:36.922 --> 00:53:39.216
- [gunshot]
- [tires screeching]

650
00:53:39.299 --> 00:53:41.593
[panting]

651
00:53:49.059 --> 00:53:49.977
[breathes deeply]

652
00:53:50.060 --> 00:53:51.520
Where you going?

653
00:53:51.603 --> 00:53:54.314
- With them.
- Don't be such a hotshot.

654
00:53:56.066 --> 00:53:57.651
Just keep your head down.

655
00:53:57.735 --> 00:53:59.319
No shit.

656
00:54:11.248 --> 00:54:13.208
I wouldn't try drivin' on.

657
00:54:13.292 --> 00:54:14.918
This guy's a good shot.

658
00:54:25.637 --> 00:54:27.431
[gunshots]

659
00:54:41.570 --> 00:54:44.031
[breathing heavily]

660
00:54:44.114 --> 00:54:46.033
Hey. [panting]

661
00:54:46.116 --> 00:54:47.117
What's going on?

662
00:54:47.201 --> 00:54:49.161
Someone in that house.

663
00:54:50.746 --> 00:54:52.372
they're stuck.

664
00:54:53.499 --> 00:54:54.583
We're stuck.

665
00:54:55.584 --> 00:54:57.377
Who do you think they are?

666
00:54:57.461 --> 00:54:58.504
Hmm.

667
00:54:59.588 --> 00:55:00.672
No idea.

668
00:55:01.840 --> 00:55:04.718
[breathing deeply]

669
00:55:04.802 --> 00:55:07.429
Hey. We're press.

670
00:55:10.432 --> 00:55:11.433
Cool.

671
00:55:13.101 --> 00:55:16.188
Now I understand why it's written
on the side of your vehicle.

672
00:55:25.155 --> 00:55:27.407
Are you WF? Who's givin' you orders?

673
00:55:28.450 --> 00:55:31.078
[sighs] No one's giving us orders. man.

674
00:55:32.454 --> 00:55:34.832
Someone's trying to Kill us.

675
00:55:34.915 --> 00:55:36.542
We're trying to kill them.

676
00:55:38.794 --> 00:55:40.921
You don't know
what side they're fighting for?

677
00:55:41.004 --> 00:55:42.798
Oh. I get it.

678
00:55:44.007 --> 00:55:45.050
You're retarded.

679
00:55:46.385 --> 00:55:48.470
You don't understand a word I say.

680
00:55:51.265 --> 00:55:54.434
- [camera shutter clicks]
- Yo! What's over there in that house?

681
00:55:54.518 --> 00:55:56.270
[whirs. clicks]

682
00:55:57.855 --> 00:55:59.189
Someone shooting.

683
00:56:02.693 --> 00:56:03.610
Guys.

684
00:56:04.570 --> 00:56:06.864
Shut the fuck up.

685
00:56:10.325 --> 00:56:13.328
[christmas music continues playing]

686
00:56:29.303 --> 00:56:30.304
[gunshot]

687
00:56:30.387 --> 00:56:31.805
- [bullet shell clinks]
- [camera clicks]

688
00:56:35.893 --> 00:56:36.935
[whirs]

689
00:56:39.897 --> 00:56:41.189
I got good news.

690
00:57:03.128 --> 00:57:04.755
[revs]

691
00:57:07.299 --> 00:57:10.510
[birds chirping]

692
00:57:16.558 --> 00:57:17.559
[taps Jessie]

693
00:57:17.643 --> 00:57:19.478
Why don't you put your head down there?

694
00:57:19.561 --> 00:57:21.939
Thanks. Sammy. I'm... good.

695
00:57:22.022 --> 00:57:24.066
Take it from an old hand.

696
00:57:24.149 --> 00:57:26.109
Sleep any chance you get.

697
00:57:26.193 --> 00:57:29.029
You never know what's coming
around the next corner.

698
00:57:31.782 --> 00:57:32.866
Yeah. all right.

699
00:57:37.746 --> 00:57:39.081
[sighs]

700
00:58:16.660 --> 00:58:18.495
- Sammy.
- What?

701
00:58:18.578 --> 00:58:20.789
Got a car comin' up on us pretty fast.

702
00:58:25.877 --> 00:58:27.462
What do you think?

703
00:58:27.546 --> 00:58:29.798
I don't know.
Maybe they're just in a hurry.

704
00:58:32.342 --> 00:58:33.760
[tires screech]

705
00:58:35.971 --> 00:58:37.931
Oh. they're in a hurry. all right.

706
00:58:38.015 --> 00:58:40.017
He smoked his tires on the last corner.

707
00:58:41.435 --> 00:58:45.022
Okay. Well. we're not gonna
outrun anyone in this thing.

708
00:58:45.105 --> 00:58:47.065
So slow down a little. Lee.

709
00:58:47.149 --> 00:58:49.317
- Let 'em pass.
- Roger that.

710
00:58:55.073 --> 00:58:58.452
[music playing loudly over speakers]

711
00:59:03.582 --> 00:59:05.417
Don't look out at 'em.

712
00:59:05.500 --> 00:59:07.377
They just roll on by.

713
00:59:13.175 --> 00:59:14.342
[music playing loudly]

714
00:59:14.426 --> 00:59:16.678
[honking]

715
00:59:16.762 --> 00:59:18.972
Oh. shit. Here we go.

716
00:59:19.056 --> 00:59:21.099
[honking]

717
00:59:21.183 --> 00:59:24.352
- [laughing]
- [continues honking]

718
00:59:24.436 --> 00:59:26.938
What the fuck? Tony?

719
00:59:27.022 --> 00:59:28.398
[panting]

720
00:59:28.482 --> 00:59:29.649
- Fuck you!
- What the fuck?

721
00:59:29.733 --> 00:59:30.734
How you guys doing?

722
00:59:31.610 --> 00:59:33.570
You just scared the shit out of me.

723
00:59:33.653 --> 00:59:35.781
Good. That was the idea.

724
00:59:35.864 --> 00:59:37.616
What the fuck are you doing here?

725
00:59:37.699 --> 00:59:40.327
I don't know. Joel.
What are you doing here?

726
00:59:41.244 --> 00:59:43.538
- [Tony laughs]
- Fuck you! Fuck youl!

727
00:59:45.624 --> 00:59:47.084
God. small world.

728
00:59:47.167 --> 00:59:49.586
Small world. my ass.
They were following us.

729
00:59:49.669 --> 00:59:51.630
Did you tell them
where we were headed back in New York?

730
00:59:51.713 --> 00:59:53.340
Fuck. no.

731
00:59:53.423 --> 00:59:57.260
Hey. Tony. did Joel tell you
where we were going back in New York?

732
00:59:57.344 --> 00:59:59.805
I don't know. Lee. He was pretty drunk

733
00:59:59.888 --> 01:00:02.140
when he was hitting on that girl
you got in the back seat.

734
01:00:03.683 --> 01:00:05.268
- Oh. for...
- You're a dick.

735
01:00:05.352 --> 01:00:07.479
Look. I must've been so wasted.

736
01:00:07.562 --> 01:00:10.524
Lee. I'm done with Bohai.

737
01:00:10.607 --> 01:00:12.734
He's lousy company.
He drives like a maniac.

738
01:00:14.653 --> 01:00:17.656
[speaks Mandarin]
[laughs]

739
01:00:18.448 --> 01:00:21.118
- Dude. what are you doing?
- I'm coming over to your car.

740
01:00:21.201 --> 01:00:22.285
- [Lee] Tony!
- [Joel] Dude!

741
01:00:23.411 --> 01:00:25.288
Are you fucking crazy. Tony?

742
01:00:25.372 --> 01:00:26.748
- Just keep the car steady.
- No!

743
01:00:26.832 --> 01:00:28.375
- Just keep it steady.
- Fuck!

744
01:00:28.458 --> 01:00:31.878
- [Joel laughs]
- Don't worry. I've done this before.

745
01:00:31.962 --> 01:00:33.380
What the fuck?

746
01:00:33.463 --> 01:00:36.091
[Tony] Just keep the car steady. Lee.
[speaks Mandarin]

747
01:00:36.174 --> 01:00:37.425
[Joel] Give me your hand.

748
01:00:38.593 --> 01:00:40.720
- [Joel laughs]
- [Jessie grunts]

749
01:00:40.804 --> 01:00:42.889
- [Sammy] You're out of your fucking mind.
- [Tony laughs]

750
01:00:42.973 --> 01:00:45.267
- You crazy bastard.
- That was so fucking...

751
01:00:45.350 --> 01:00:47.686
So fucking sick! [laughs]

752
01:00:48.395 --> 01:00:49.437
I gotta do it.

753
01:00:49.521 --> 01:00:50.438
What?

754
01:00:50.522 --> 01:00:51.690
I'm doing it.

755
01:00:51.773 --> 01:00:53.066
[Joel] Jesus. Lee.

756
01:00:53.150 --> 01:00:54.151
Don't turn the wheel.

757
01:00:58.530 --> 01:01:01.783
My new passenger.
Much better. much better.

758
01:01:01.867 --> 01:01:03.493
- Pull over.
- Bye-bye. Tony.

759
01:01:03.577 --> 01:01:04.995
Bye-bye. See you in Washington.

760
01:01:05.078 --> 01:01:06.413
Fuck you!

761
01:01:06.496 --> 01:01:09.374
[revving]

762
01:01:09.457 --> 01:01:11.251
[laughing]

763
01:01:13.670 --> 01:01:16.506
[music playing loudly]

764
01:01:21.428 --> 01:01:22.429
[laughing]

765
01:01:22.512 --> 01:01:23.930
I told you he drives like a maniac.

766
01:01:24.014 --> 01:01:25.348
[continues laughing]

767
01:01:31.104 --> 01:01:32.189
Where did they go?

768
01:01:42.949 --> 01:01:44.326
This feel funny?

769
01:01:45.035 --> 01:01:46.703
Where did your guy go. Tony?

770
01:01:47.495 --> 01:01:49.372
He's just fucking around. that's all.

771
01:01:49.456 --> 01:01:50.957
I don't want him fuckin' around.

772
01:01:51.041 --> 01:01:52.709
I want Jessie back in this car.

773
01:01:52.792 --> 01:01:55.629
Relax. Lee. He's just showing
how fast he can drive. The girl's fine.

774
01:01:55.712 --> 01:01:58.173
How the fuck do you know if she's fine?
Can you see her?

775
01:01:58.256 --> 01:02:00.383
- [horn blaring]
- Whoa!

776
01:02:00.467 --> 01:02:02.177
[tires screeching]

777
01:02:04.179 --> 01:02:05.764
- [Joel] Fuck!
- [grunts]

778
01:02:07.849 --> 01:02:09.476
[brakes screech]

779
01:02:16.691 --> 01:02:17.901
Oh. fuck.

780
01:02:22.864 --> 01:02:24.199
[tires screeching]

781
01:02:36.836 --> 01:02:41.841
[birds chirping]

782
01:03:00.235 --> 01:03:01.236
Shit.

783
01:03:55.248 --> 01:03:57.709
[inaudible]

784
01:04:05.133 --> 01:04:06.259
[breathes heavily]

785
01:04:33.244 --> 01:04:34.329
[sighs]

786
01:04:34.412 --> 01:04:36.206
We need to go down there. Now.

787
01:04:36.289 --> 01:04:38.833
If we go down there.
they're going to Kill us.

788
01:04:38.917 --> 01:04:40.210
No.

789
01:04:40.293 --> 01:04:42.921
Those aren't government forces.
Not up here.

790
01:04:43.004 --> 01:04:45.131
